WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:08.560
This video gives a brief introduction to the Arclight device.

2
00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:12.520
Switch it on using this grey button.

3
00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:18.440
At first, both ends of the Arclight may come on at the same time.

4
00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:24.580
If it does not come on at all or the lights are dim, the battery may be flat.

5
00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:27.360
Plug it in using the USB charger.

6
00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:31.240
When charging, the green lights will come on.

7
00:00:31.790 --> 00:00:37.510
After 15 minutes, it should be fully charged and work for several hours.

8
00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:41.390
Leaving it in sunlight will keep the battery charged.

9
00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:44.970
You will not need to replace any batteries or bulbs.

10
00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:49.090
The mode when both ends come on is for general use.

11
00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:54.980
Switch to eye mode by holding the button down for 15 seconds.

12
00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:59.920
Then lift your fingers and quickly press again as the light flashes.

13
00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:04.560
You are now in eye mode, where the ophthalmoscope will come on

14
00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:07.940
first, then the anterior segment loupe.

15
00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:13.960
Repeating these steps will cycle through three different modes of use.

16
00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:15.740
General use, eyes, then ears.

17
00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:20.080
Once you have selected the preferred mode, pressing the grey button

18
00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:25.520
changes how bright the lights are and which end is lit.

19
00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:30.140
Make sure you use the correct end for the correct examination.

20
00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:34.700
The external eye is examined by using the loupe.

21
00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:41.140
The view will be clear when you are very close to the eye at around 6 cm.

22
00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:48.300
The fundal reflex is performed at arm's length using the direct ophthalmoscope.

23
00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:53.740
If the view is blurred, then check the lens rack is at the top.

24
00:01:54.160 --> 00:02:00.540
In this position, there is no lens in the sight hole and the reflex should be clear.

25
00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:50.180
The Arclight can also be used to capture video of clinical signs

26
00:02:50.180 --> 00:02:53.760
when attached to the camera of a mobile phone.

27
00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:57.810
Once attached, the sight hole of the direct ophthalmoscope

28
00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:05.920
will be placed directly over the centre of the lens that your mobile camera uses in video mode.

29
00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:11.800
The camera will function just like your eyes when you are looking through the sight hole.

30
00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:15.720
To confirm which lens to line up the sight hole with,

31
00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:21.760
open the video app on your phone, place your finger over each lens in turn.

32
00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:27.100
When the screen goes dark, you have covered the lens used for video.

33
00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:31.960
Remove the yellow paper from the back of the clip.

34
00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:38.180
Place the points of the arrow over the centre of the lens used to capture video.

35
00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:41.040
Press the clip down firmly.

36
00:03:41.870 --> 00:03:43.150
Remove the arrow.

37
00:03:44.210 --> 00:03:47.410
The clip should now be in the correct position.

38
00:03:47.650 --> 00:03:51.470
To video the reflex, switch on the direct ophthalmoscope

39
00:03:51.690 --> 00:03:56.770
end of the Arclight and select the brightest light with three clicks.

40
00:03:57.090 --> 00:03:59.310
Make sure the lens rack is at the top.

41
00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:03.820
With the light facing away from the phone towards the patient,

42
00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:09.840
place the Arclight in the clip and pull the elastic over to secure.

43
00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:14.840
Push the Arclight up until it cannot slide any further.

44
00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:17.380
The sight hole of the direct ophthalmoscope

45
00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:23.560
will now be directly over the centre of the lens that captures video.

46
00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:28.460
To record the external eye, use the other end of the device.

47
00:04:28.460 --> 00:04:34.160
To capture images, open the video app and zoom in,

48
00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:38.020
filling the screen with the view through the sight hole.

49
00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:41.000
Press record and perform the examination.

50
00:04:41.480 --> 00:04:43.220
Press stop and save the video.

51
00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:48.200
You can now share with colleagues on secure, encrypted platforms

52
00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:53.260
only for the purpose for which you gained consent from the patient.

53
00:05:16.990 --> 00:05:19.890
Enjoy using the Arclight in your work.

